INT. FERRY SNACK BAR - NIGHT

A rolling sea outside the salt-streaked windows. Fluorescent lights buzz. Plastic chairs are bolted to the floor.

MAEVE LINDQVIST, 30s, rain jacket, clutches a paper cup. DESMOND OKAFOR, 30s, rumpled suit, stands across the counter from her, a ring box in his fist.

DESMOND
I had a speech.

MAEVE
You always have a speech.

GUS TREMBLAY, 60s, the snack bar attendant, wipes the counter and pretends to be deaf.

DESMOND
Maeve, the ferry leaves the dock in nine minutes. If you're getting off--

MAEVE
I'm not getting off.

DESMOND
Then why'd you text me?

PRIYA RAMANATHAN, 20s, Maeve's sister, bursts through the door, soaked, suitcase in tow.

PRIYA
Because she's an idiot, that's why!

MAEVE
Priya!

GUS
(to nobody)
I'll just be over here.

DESMOND
You told your sister?

PRIYA
She told me everything. The ring, the job in Oslo, the--

MAEVE
Stop talking.

PRIYA
--the fact you cried in a car wash.

MAEVE
It was a very sad car wash!

DESMOND
Wait, Oslo?

The ferry lurches. Desmond and Maeve grab the counter at the same time. Their hands land together. Both freeze. Priya gasps. Gus drops his rag.

PRIYA
Oh my God. Kiss her, you coward.

DESMOND
Maeve, are you leaving?

MAEVE
I was asked to. I said no. I just didn't tell you.

GUS
Smart girl.

ODALYS FERREIRA, 50s, in a captain's cap and a stained apron, shoulders in with a tray of lemon cake. She stops.

ODALYS
Who ordered the proposal?

Desmond drops to one knee. The ring box pops open. A huge wave slams the hull, and the lemon cake lands on Priya's suitcase.

DESMOND
Marry me or I throw up, I swear to God.

MAEVE
Yes! Yes, get up!

Priya shrieks. Gus applauds. Odalys snatches the ring box and examines it.

ODALYS
Cheap setting. Good stone.

Desmond stands. Maeve grabs his collar. They kiss as the ship horn blasts.
